---
/**
 * The hero (docs/projects/redesign/design-export/README.md §1, "Hero").
 *
 * The H1 is the name and nothing else — no job title in a headline (constraint
 * 1), no eyebrow above it (constraint 2). The only decorative motion on the
 * whole page lives here.
 *
 * THE HERO'S TYPE AND LAYOUT ARE `.rd-hero` IN global.css, shared with the other
 * eight heroes: the H1, the 32ch lede, the row, the right block's hairline shell
 * and the 720px collapse. What stays here is this hero's own right-block
 * content — the agent pointer — and the padding above the headline.
 *
 * RETRO RESTYLES THIS SAME MARKUP under
 * `html[data-appearance='retro'] [data-module='home-hero']` in retro.css. The
 * module prefix there is what buys those rules the one extra attribute they
 * need to outweigh the Astro-scoped selectors below, whose
 * `[data-astro-cid-…]` counts as a class. Nothing here is appearance-aware.
 */
---

<section class="rd-section rd-hero hero" data-module="home-hero">
  <h1>
    Matt{' '}
    {/*
      THE HERO FILL — `.rd-fill` in global.css, shared with the /writing and
      post headlines. It defaults to the agents magenta, which is the colour
      this headline wants; the two writing surfaces add `.rd-fill--writing`.
    */}
    <span class="rd-fill">Pyle</span>
  </h1>

  <div class="hero-row">
    <p class="hero-statement">
      This site is an experiment in building the web for its newest readers, and publishing what
      they see.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-aside hero-agent">
      <span class="hero-agent-copy">Reading this as an agent?<br />Start here.</span>
      <a href="/llms.txt" class="hero-agent-link">llms.txt</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: 78px; }

  .hero-agent { gap: 10px; }

  .hero-agent-copy {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ink-5);
  }

  .hero-agent-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono-plex);
    font-size: 19px;
    color: var(--agents);
  }

  .hero-agent-link:hover { color: var(--agents-hover); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .hero { padding-top: 40px; }

    /* One inline row on mobile, per the 390px prototype. The shared collapse
       stacks the block's children in a column; this hero is the one that wants
       its label and link on one line. */
    .hero .hero-agent {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: baseline;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 14px;
    }

    .hero-agent-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 44px;
      padding: 10px 0;
      font-size: 18px;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
  }
</style>
